  "details": "https://vrchatevents.com/   :(   I'm not overly active in VRChat, but have an art opening in NYC to share (and a presentation in VRChat that I'm apparently best able to share outside of VRChat - lol, sigh) ... I've been part of many communities over the years, so I get the why and how here. Yet, it begs the question - Is VRChat a Clubhouse?  There's a general vibe of this across the platform.  (This path often happens when smart hard working people make something with passion and not much pay then give it for free.   Its great, yet there's always downsides - reality may push a more business-like approach)",
